<AppDocs app={stampShift} active="privacy" title="Stamp Shift privacy policy" description="How Stamp Shift stores local progress, handles Apple purchases, and shares optional puzzle information." heading="Privacy at the desk." intro="Stamp Shift is made by Jordan Blum. This policy covers the app, purchases, optional support messages and these documentation pages.">
  <p class="docs-caption">Last updated October 16, 2026</p>
  <section><h2>Progress stays on this device.</h2><p>Stamp Shift saves your current route, move history, delivered routes and sound/haptic settings in local device storage (UserDefaults). The app has no in-app accounts, analytics, advertising, developer backend or cloud sync.</p><p>Deleting the app can remove local progress. I do not maintain a developer-hosted copy of your progress.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Apple handles payment.</h2><p>Extra Routes is a permanent in-app purchase. Stamp Shift uses Apple's StoreKit to check verified purchase entitlements and unlock the pack. I do not receive your payment-card details through the app.</p><p>Apple's purchase and account services follow <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>. Restoring purchases may require a connection to Apple and the Apple Account used for the purchase.</p></section>
  <section><h2>You choose what to share.</h2><p><strong>Share puzzle information</strong> in Help &amp; privacy opens Apple's native share sheet. The text includes the route identifier and title, manifest progress, move count and move history, and app version/build. It does not include account or payment details. No puzzle report is sent to me automatically.</p><p>You choose whether to send the text and which app or person receives it. Those recipients may have their own privacy policies.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Support is handled by email.</h2><p>If you email me, I receive your message, the contact information you provide, and any puzzle information or attachments you choose to include. I use that information to reply and investigate the issue. Please don't send passwords or payment details.</p><p>Support email uses Gmail, so messages are also handled by Google under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">its privacy policy</a>. Email me to request deletion of information you sent; I will review the request and explain any information that needs to be retained. This does not remove copies held by your email provider or other recipients.</p></section>
  <section><h2>About these documentation pages</h2><p>These app documentation pages are static and do not load the personal site's chat assistant. They have no analytics, advertising, forms or client-side JavaScript. Reading them does not send a chat message or puzzle report.</p><p>The site is delivered using Amazon Web Services S3 and CloudFront. Serving a webpage requires processing request information such as the requested URL, IP address, browser information and request time. Hosting services may keep operational logs under their own settings and policies; this is separate from the app's local progress. See <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/privacy/">AWS's privacy notice</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Questions about privacy</h2><p class="docs-contact">Contact Jordan Blum at <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}?subject=Stamp%20Shift%20privacy`}>{supportEmail}</a> about this policy or information you chose to send to support.</p></section>
</AppDocs>
